id: relationship-projection:dave:christianity:public-safe
title: "Dave / Christianity public-safe relationship projection"
kind: relationship-projection
record_shape: public-projection
status: draft
lifecycle: proposed
projection_revision: 1
canonical_relationship_ref: relationship:dave:christianity
canonical_relationship_revision: 2
canonical_schema_ref: schemas/relationship.v0.1.schema.json
participation_schema_ref: schemas/participation.v0.1.schema.json
relation_address_schema_ref: schemas/relation-address.v0.1.schema.json
inference_envelope_schema_ref: schemas/inference-envelope.v0.1.schema.json
relationship_view_contract_ref: interface/relationship-view-v0.1.yawn
privacy: public-safe
public_projection: dave/christianity/
principal_ref: principal:dave
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Codex session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-30; a public-safe conformance record built from Dave's stated request. It does not establish Dave's identity, beliefs, consent beyond this publication request, or a shared religious conclusion."
created: 2026-09-30
updated: 2026-09-30

projection:
  disclosure_scope: public-safe
  basis: >
    This is the permitted public projection of canonical
    relationship:dave:christianity at revision 2. It materializes only the
    fields allowed by this record's public-safe boundary.
  withheld:
    - private_inference_envelopes_and_persisted_outputs
    - private_reflections_and_unapproved_personal_belief_claims
    - private_conversation_material_and_third_party_personal_information
  rule: >
    This projection is a View, not a second canonical relationship record. A
    public reader can inspect the displayed purpose, boundaries, sources, and
    frontier without receiving private inference output or authority.

purpose:
  text: >
    Inspect the model Dave is carrying around Christianity, distinguish
    attributed sources from interpretation, preserve uncertainty and
    disagreement, and identify a useful next question without forcing a
    religious identity, conclusion, or action.
  asserted_by: principal:dave
  epistemic_status: reported
  lifecycle: proposed

referents:
  - ref: principal:dave
    kind: principal
    relationship_role: anchor
  - ref: tradition:christianity
    kind: tradition
    relationship_role: inquiry_target

participation:
  - participant_ref: principal:dave
    role: principal
    presence: present
    standpoint: first_person
    authority: may_correct_or_withhold_own_report
    epistemic_status: reported
  - participant_ref: agents:yawn.bot
    role: observer
    presence: present
    standpoint: proposal_only
    authority: none
    epistemic_status: reported

stewardship:
  yawn_ref: null
  status: not_assigned
  rule: >
    This Relationship has not yet been promoted to or assigned a Yawn steward.
    A later proposal must establish an independent continuity, inquiry, proof,
    maintenance, authority, or privacy need; it cannot create a Yawn or grant
    authority merely by naming one.

represented_voices:
  rule: >
    Historical figures, text authors, traditions, scholars, and interpreters
    may be referenced through attributed sources or modeled perspectives. They
    are not current participants, consenting parties, decision holders, or
    authorities merely because a record quotes or represents them.
  default_status: source_associated_or_simulated_only

coupling:
  current: >
    Dave's inquiry is mediated by source materials, interpretations, memories,
    conversations, and this revisable record. This describes a modelled
    relationship, not a claim that the tradition or any historical person is
    currently interacting with Dave.
  channels:
    - source_reading
    - attributed_interpretation
    - participant_reflection
    - yawn_proposal_only
  boundary: "Possible influence is distinct from permitted action, authority, commitment, or proof."

boundaries:
  must_not:
    - "Infer or publish Dave's religious identity, beliefs, commitments, or private history."
    - "Treat a source-attributed statement as a verified statement by a historical person without preserving the attribution chain."
    - "Treat historical, textual, simulated, or quoted voices as live participants."
    - "Treat dave/christianity or dave/christianity/jesus as containment, agreement, consent, identity, or authority."
    - "Turn a relationship address, source popularity, model fluency, or perspective count into proof."
    - "Allow Yawn, whether observing now or proposed as a future steward, to ratify Dave's positions or make external commitments."
  public_safe_fields:
    - stated_purpose
    - protocol_boundaries
    - publicly_named_source_references
    - explicitly_authorized_public_questions
  withheld_by_default:
    - private_reflections
    - unapproved_personal_belief_claims
    - private_conversation_material
    - third_party_personal_information

relation_address:
  display_path: dave/christianity
  anchor_ref: principal:dave
  target_ref: tradition:christianity
  direction: forward
  semantics: directional_view
  relation_ref: relationship:dave:christianity
  path_proves_parentage: false
  path_proves_identity: false
  path_proves_agreement: false
  path_proves_consent: false
  path_grants_authority: false
  note: >
    A later address such as dave/christianity/jesus must declare each typed
    relation step and remains a traversal/View, not containment. It does not
    establish Dave's belief about Jesus or make a historical subject a live
    participant.

views:
  - id: purpose
    question: "Why is this relationship open?"
  - id: model
    question: "What model, assumptions, and lacunae are currently visible?"
  - id: perspectives
    question: "Which attributed perspectives, alternatives, and disagreements bear on the question?"
  - id: sources
    question: "What does each source report, and what is interpretation?"
  - id: boundaries
    question: "Who is participating, what is private, and what may happen here?"
  - id: history
    question: "What changed in the representation, when, and on what evidence?"
  - id: frontier
    question: "What question, hold, or small inspection would most change orientation now?"

frontier:
  status: open
  current_question: "Which source-bounded question about Christianity would most change Dave's present orientation, and why?"
  selection_basis:
    - stated_purpose
    - source_and_attribution_boundary
    - unresolved_scope
    - no_inferred_personal_position
  allowed_next_moves:
    - name_a_specific_source_or_question
    - distinguish_source_from_interpretation
    - compare_attributed_perspectives
    - record_a_personal_report_if_dave_explicitly_supplies_one
    - hold
  disallowed_next_moves:
    - infer_belief_or_identity
    - create_an_external_commitment
    - publish_private_material

history:
  - event: public_projection_materialized
    recorded_at: 2026-09-30
    actor_ref: agent:codex
    basis: "Participant-requested public-safe conformance case; canonical relationship revision 2."
    epistemic_status: reported
    effect: "Materializes the permitted public View without exposing private inference output, belief, agreement, or external action."

sources:
  - ref: fixtures/relationship-core.v0.1.json
    description: "Canonical Relationship Core conformance fixture containing relationship:dave:christianity revision 2 and its private inference-envelope boundary."
    epistemic_status: observed
  - ref: agents/yawn.bot.yawn
    description: "YAWN.bot's declared proposal-only runtime identity and authority boundary."
    epistemic_status: observed
  - ref: participant-request:relationship-pressure-test:2026-09-30
    description: "Dave requested this public-safe conformance case and supplied the desired relationship-first distinctions."
    epistemic_status: reported
  - ref: spec/ontology.md
    description: "Relationship is a situated, changing coupling and does not automatically establish containment, agreement, or authority."
    epistemic_status: observed
  - ref: core/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_AGENT_ARENA.yawn
    description: "Relationship is structurally first and Observation is operationally first."
    epistemic_status: observed

proof:
  condition: >
    The public projection identifies its canonical relationship and revision,
    lets a reader inspect the permitted purpose, boundary, source attribution,
    active lacunae, and current frontier, and withholds private inference
    output, unprovided belief, identity, private reflection, and false live
    participation claims.
  falsifier: >
    The record or View implies that Dave believes a doctrine, treats a
    historical source as a present participant, makes path nesting mean
    containment, or allows an unapproved external action.
  status: not_started
